From 533e3d73f36946ff719a2e95ec54208590bd763a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:01:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freebsd: additional_devices and the Devices annotation unhide
 devices in devfs

internal/config/device had only a stub off Linux: additional_devices and
io.kubernetes.cri-o.Devices were accepted and ignored. On FreeBSD parse
them with the Linux syntax (the parser moves to parse.go), check that
each device is on the host's devfs and keeps its own path, and unhide it
in the container's devfs like CRI devices. The access mode is accepted
but devfs has no per-container modes: the node's own mode applies.
---
